    "title": "Woman suspected of threatening people with knife in Santa Rosa shopping center",
    "text": "Officers used a stun gun to arrest a woman accused of threatening people with a “large knife” in a Santa Rosa shopping center, police said Monday, April 13. The woman is suspected of making criminal threats, brandishing a weapon and resisting officers, according to the Santa Rosa Police Department. She was being held at the Sonoma County jail Monday in lieu of $30,000 bail. Officers arrested the woman after they got reports of threats taking place about 9:45 a.m. Sunday, April 12, outside Safeway at Mendocino Avenue and Steele Lane. Callers told dispatchers a woman was trying to stab people and chasing them in the street, police said. Officers found her across the street in a Chase Bank parking lot, where she is accused of pointing a knife at them and telling them to stay back. A 10-minute encounter forced officials to shut down southbound Mendocino Avenue with medical personnel staged nearby. Officers used “a less-lethal projectile” that had no effect before deploying a stun gun that allowed them to take the woman into custody, police said. They confiscated the knife and the woman was taken to a local hospital for minor injuries, officials said. No other injuries were reported and the road reopened shortly after. You can reach Staff Writer Colin Atagi at colin.atagi@pressdemocrat.com. %5B%7B%22id%22%3A3040%2C%22name%22%3A%22Breaking%20News%20Alerts%22%2C%22description%22%3A%22First%20and%20factual.%20Get%20the%20details%20you%20need%20from%20the%20PD%20newsroom%20team.%22%7D%5DFirst and factual. Get the details you need from the PD newsroom team.RevContent Feed",
